        "x1": 0.6060503278459821,
        "y1": 0.5110451886319775
      },
      "text": "−r+1",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6098824124376313,
        "y0": 0.502792308562725,
        "x1": 0.8813447840073529,
        "y1": 0.5157484838345272
      },
      "text": "log n (cf. Theorem 3.5). A natural",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919329987854517,
        "y0": 0.5187537992935,
        "x1": 0.8813450917476365,
        "y1": 0.5317099745653021
      },
      "text": "question, which was asked in [20], is to determine the correct threshold (depending on r, q) for",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919196633731617,
        "y0": 0.5348588168762642,
        "x1": 0.8809420545561975,
        "y1": 0.5478149921480664
      },
      "text": "the property of having a perfect matching with high discrepancy in every q-colouring. Motivated",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919212020745798,
        "y0": 0.5509631095759375,
        "x1": 0.8811429063813025,
        "y1": 0.5639192848477397
      },
      "text": "by this, we prove the following result, which starts working at the threshold for the existence",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919212020745798,
        "y0": 0.5670678734496201,
        "x1": 0.8813431427258404,
        "y1": 0.5800240487214222
      },
      "text": "of a perfect matching, and even yields an asymptotically optimal bound on the discrepancy.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919212020745798,
        "y0": 0.5831721661492935,
        "x1": 0.881142803801208,
        "y1": 0.5961283414210956
      },
      "text": "However, note that we assume the colouring is known a priori, that is, the statement we prove",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919212020745798,
        "y0": 0.5992769300229759,
        "x1": 0.4215109432444853,
        "y1": 0.612233105294778
      },
      "text": "to hold w.h.p. is for a fixed colouring.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919212020745798,
        "y0": 0.6246448661822321,
        "x1": 0.24322612345719538,
        "y1": 0.6376010414540343
      },
      "text": "Theorem 1.4.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2527050627379858,
        "y0": 0.6246448661822321,
        "x1": 0.7526532597902442,
        "y1": 0.6376010414540343
      },
      "text": "For all r, q ∈ N with r, q ≥ 2, and all µ > 0, there exists C",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7619487858620011,
        "y0": 0.6246448661822321,
        "x1": 0.8811418805803571,
        "y1": 0.6376010414540343
      },
      "text": "> 0 such that,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919227407759979,
        "y0": 0.6407496300559146,
        "x1": 0.2518985010996586,
        "y1": 0.6537058053277167
      },
      "text": "provided p ≥ Cn",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2518984241645877,
        "y0": 0.6395368213608259,
        "x1": 0.28799941119025735,
        "y1": 0.6490025101251671
      },
      "text": "−r+1",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2916293104155725,
        "y0": 0.6407496300559146,
        "x1": 0.4962989101890756,
        "y1": 0.6537058053277167
      },
      "text": "log n, the following holds.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5058148552389706,
        "y0": 0.6407496300559146,
        "x1": 0.8813443736869748,
        "y1": 0.6537058053277167
      },
      "text": "For any q-colouring of the k-subsets of [n], the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919335116859243,
        "y0": 0.6567113744957713,
        "x1": 0.33015049525669643,
        "y1": 0.6696675497675735
      },
      "text": "random hypergraph G ∼ G",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.33015100815716913,
        "y0": 0.6554990369746917,
        "x1": 0.3478987493434874,
        "y1": 0.6649647257390328
      },
      "text": "(r)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.3489075476381959,
        "y0": 0.6567113744957713,
        "x1": 0.8343519451237527,
        "y1": 0.6696675497675735
      },
      "text": "(n, p) contains w.h.p. a perfect matching with at least (1 − µ)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8363697725183824,
        "y0": 0.6647623542368837,
        "x1": 0.8621851816898635,
        "y1": 0.6742280430012247
      },
      "text": "r+n",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8543194939108456,
        "y0": 0.6647623542368837,
        "x1": 0.8793280593487395,
        "y1": 0.6742280430012247
      },
      "text": "q−1",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919360761882879,
        "y0": 0.6728157034395993,
        "x1": 0.3196638347721901,
        "y1": 0.6857718787114014
      },
      "text": "edges of the same colour.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919360761882879,
        "y0": 0.7112955061670154,
        "x1": 0.6135507279083509,
        "y1": 0.7242516814388176
      },
      "text": "Organisation. The rest of the paper is organised as follows.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6229931743205095,
        "y0": 0.7112955061670154,
        "x1": 0.8813466304490546,
        "y1": 0.7242516814388176
      },
      "text": "The proof of the defect theorem",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919396664915967,
        "y0": 0.7274002519186206,
        "x1": 0.8813445788471639,
        "y1": 0.7403564271904227
      },
      "text": "(Theorem 1.3) is discussed in Section 2 and the proof of the transference theorem (Theorem 1.2)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919329987854517,
        "y0": 0.7435043996416758,
        "x1": 0.2226921273880646,
        "y1": 0.756460574913478
      },
      "text": "in Section 3.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.23637000332359506,
        "y0": 0.7435046352286803,
        "x1": 0.6454145671940651,
        "y1": 0.7564608105004824
      },
      "text": "The proof of Theorem 1.4 is also discussed there.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6590921866793592,
        "y0": 0.7435046352286803,
        "x1": 0.8813445788471639,
        "y1": 0.7564608105004824
      },
      "text": "Finally, we give concluding",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919327423352154,
        "y0": 0.7594668689646233,
        "x1": 0.8813449122324711,
        "y1": 0.7724230442364255
      },
      "text": "remarks in Section 4. The proof of the multicolour weak sparse hypergraph regularity lemma is",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919329987854517,
        "y0": 0.775570907955215,
        "x1": 0.43563027261685927,
        "y1": 0.7885270832270171
      },
      "text": "added for completeness in Appendix A.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6258149988511029,
        "y0": 0.8030047903717838,
        "x1": 0.6435627400374212,
        "y1": 0.8124704791361249
      },
      "text": "(r)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919329987854517,
        "y0": 0.8063548806161043,
        "x1": 0.20692446412158613,
        "y1": 0.8193110558879064
      },
      "text": "Notation.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2164030443720457,
        "y0": 0.8063548806161043,
        "x1": 0.5401376419708508,
        "y1": 0.8193110558879064
      },
      "text": "We use standard graph theory notation.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5499831768644958,
        "y0": 0.8063548806161043,
        "x1": 0.6244030864298844,
        "y1": 0.8193110558879064
      },
      "text": "We let K",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6244028299796481,
        "y0": 0.8115558556309789,
        "x1": 0.6330751050420168,
        "y1": 0.8210215443953199
      },
      "text": "n",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6510250315946691,
        "y0": 0.8063548806161043,
        "x1": 0.8815462513130252,
        "y1": 0.8193110558879064
      },
      "text": "denote the complete r-graph",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1191932485884979,
        "y0": 0.8224596263677094,
        "x1": 0.22668892996651785,
        "y1": 0.8354158016395116
      },
      "text": "on n vertices.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8518993217404149,
        "y0": 0.8280179574200772,
        "x1": 0.860369873046875,
        "y1": 0.8409741326918795
      },
      "text": "(",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8728742327008928,
        "y0": 0.828017939298,
        "x1": 0.8813447840073529,
        "y1": 0.8409741145698022
      },
      "text": ")",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1476300536083574,
        "y0": 0.8385643721193146,
        "x1": 0.845043034914161,
        "y1": 0.8515205473911167
      },
      "text": "We let [n] denote the set {1, . . . , n} and, given a set X and an integer i ≥ 0, we write",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8601680980009191,
        "y0": 0.8362112498340017,
        "x1": 0.8718655626313025,
        "y1": 0.8456769385983429
      },
      "text": "X",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.8642017011882878,
        "y0": 0.8464728036006103,
        "x1": 0.8690420455291492,
        "y1": 0.8559384923649513
      },
      "text": "i",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919355632878151,
        "y0": 0.8545261346812486,
        "x1": 0.4806053353958771,
        "y1": 0.8674823099530508
      },
      "text": "for the collection of all subsets of X of size i.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.14763055368631828,
        "y0": 0.8706308804328537,
        "x1": 0.8811453683035714,
        "y1": 0.8835870557046559
      },
      "text": "For a, b, c ∈ (0, 1], we write a ≪ b ≪ c in our statements to mean that there are increasing",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1191930947183561,
        "y0": 0.8867351550104499,
        "x1": 0.8815465590533088,
        "y1": 0.8996913302822521
      },
      "text": "functions f, g : (0, 1] → (0, 1] such that whenever a ≤ f (b) and b ≤ g(c), then the subsequent",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11919371019892332,
        "y0": 0.9028399007620551,
        "x1": 0.21721088826155463,
        "y1": 0.9157960760338573
      },
      "text": "result holds.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.495731539686187,
        "y0": 0.9364739868816457,
        "x1": 0.5048071596802783,
        "y1": 0.9494301621534479
      },
      "text": "3",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
